proof.text:
Let $L$ and $R$ denote the two displayed system composites in the statement, with $c,J,\xi$ replaced by $a,b,x$. Both go from $T_{Y'}G_{g,A}\mathscr P_{f,A}M_\bullet$ to $\mathscr P_{f',B}G_{g',B}T_XM_\bullet$. Compute their adjuncts using Steps 2--3 and naturality of $\eta$:
$$U(L)\eta_{G_{g,A}\mathscr P_{f,A}M_\bullet}
=\mathscr P_{f',A}G_{g',A}(\eta_{M_\bullet})\,x_{A,M_\bullet},$$
$$U(R)\eta_{G_{g,A}\mathscr P_{f,A}M_\bullet}
=x_{A,U_XT_XM_\bullet}\,G_{g,A}\mathscr P_{f,A}(\eta_{M_\bullet}).$$
For the first formula, naturality of $\eta$ moves it across $T(x_A)$, the $a_{f'}$ adjunct replaces $U(a_{f'})\eta$ by $\mathscr P_{f',A}(\eta)$, and the $b_{g'}$ adjunct replaces the remaining unit by $G_{g',A}(\eta)$. For the second, first use the $b_g$ adjunct, then the $a_f$ adjunct, and finally $U(x_B)=x_{A,U(-)}$. The two displayed maps agree by naturality of the natural transformation $x_A$ at $\eta_{M_\bullet}$. The bijection $\operatorname{Hom}(TQ,N)\cong\operatorname{Hom}(Q,UN)$ now gives $L=R$ in the derived category of entire $B_\bullet$-systems. No faithfulness of $U$ or of evaluation is needed.
